From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:31:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 259/259] CED state: declare the sink detector's column scatter

A compacted decoder scatters the attention-sink detector's columns
([tokens, hc_mult] float32, vLLM 0221) back to every row. The CED ports declared
that layout only under pipeline parallelism, where a stage's pre-mix has the
same shape: they were qualified on r6x, before the detector existed. On
spark-ds41f-1022 the first TP4 boot stopped in memory profiling with
"TileLang kernel 'ced_copy_rows' was not prepared ... copy_rows_kernel('float32',
(4,), (1,), True, True)".

CEDState.warmup takes sink_columns, set from the model's
get_sink_residual_columns(), and declares the float32 [hc_mult] scatter when the
model keeps the columns or under pipeline parallelism.

Test: with sink_columns the frozen cache serves the columns' scatter without a
compile; without it the same scatter is refused by name.
